quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1046705-dark-eras-mother-wolf-for-norse-uratha?p=1223262#post1223262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small dictionary of local terms I use for Norse Uratha, in context of Mother of Wolves myth.<br /> <br /> <b>Luna / Moon</b> \u2013 <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%A1ni\" target=\"_blank\">Mani</a></i>, Father Moon<br /> <b>Urfarah / Wolf</b> - <i>Mother of Wolves</i>, later <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angrbo%C3%B0a\" target=\"_blank\">Angerboda</a></i> - One Who Brings Grief<br /> <b>Sun</b> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%B3l_(sun)\" target=\"_blank\">S\u00f3l</a><br /> <b>Lunes</b> - <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hj%C3%BAki_and_Bil\" target=\"_blank\">Hjukis</a></i>, rarely <i>Bils</i><br /> <b>Forsaken</b> - <i>De \u00d6vergivna</i><br /> <b>Pure </b>- <i>De Rena</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to point out that an important aspect of Werewolf lore is that Wolf is long dead. Angerboda isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T14:42:05-07:00","id":1223728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1046705-dark-eras-mother-wolf-for-norse-uratha?p=1223726#post1223726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to point out that an important aspect of Werewolf lore is that Wolf is long dead. Angerboda isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there direct myths on this? I do know she is only Mother of Many Monsters. Mother do not need to live past birthing the children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T01:33:41-07:00","id":1224110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1046705-dark-eras-mother-wolf-for-norse-uratha?p=1223728#post1223728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are there direct myths on this? I do know she is only Mother of Many Monsters. Mother do not need to live past birthing the children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Hel, the Midgard Serpent, and Fenrir were living with her. in her home, where Loki visited her, while he carried on the tryst with her.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T19:31:13-07:00","id":1233887,"title":"","content":"Here is my take on Uratha, Vikings and Norse mythology: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1191264-the-wolf-age-my-wtf-dark-ages-campaign\">The Wolf Age</a><br /> <br /> Mani is sexually dimorphic, just like in regular forsaken mythology. Uratha usually see Mani as a mother.<br /> <br /> Father Wolf, is Fenrir, who is distinct from and the father of Fenris-Ur the Firstborn.<br /> <br /> Fenrir, was slain by his children which caused the Sundering. But he hadn't fulfilled his fate yet, so the Norns would just return him to life. Before he resurrected, Tyr drug him into the Underworld and chained him up. There he remains separated from Midgard and it's Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","user":"Jeremysbrain","date":". 07-10-2018, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}